			"notes": "Dead mobs are now real physics bodies instead of playing a fixed animation.\n\n- **Physics bodies.** A dying mob becomes rigid parts joined at its joints. It falls, tumbles, slides and comes to rest on whatever blocks are there: stairs, slabs, fences, walls. Armor and held items follow.\n- **The killing blow matters.** Melee hits knock the body back; Knockback, sprint hits and Punch throw it further. Arrows hit the part they pass through. Creepers and TNT fling bodies away and walls block the blast. A mace smash drives the body down.\n- **Dying muscles.** For about a second and a half the body braces and reaches, then goes limp.\n- **Water and lava.** Bodies float and drift with the current; soul sand bubble columns lift them fast, magma ones slowly. Lava burns black exactly the pixels that touched it.\n- **Materials.** Bodies slide far on ice, bounce on slime, hang in cobwebs and sink into powder snow.\n- **Special mobs.** Skeletons break apart, a snow golem's pumpkin rolls off, blaze and breeze rods drop free, spiders flip and curl.\n- **Sounds and dust.** Thuds, splashes and bone clatter, heard only by you.\n- **Settings.** A new Physics section; turning Physics Bodies off brings back the 1.0 animations.\n- Fixed: on 26.1.x a render hook did not apply, so limb and armor posing could fail."
		},
